WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Linen is woven from flax.

2
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:05.070
Rope is made from hemp and jute.

3
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.680
All three come from plant stems.

4
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:12.830
Picture a single thin fibre that
holds 4 kilograms before it snaps.

5
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.660
Yet a stem is built from cells, and
their walls are made of cellulose:

6
00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:19.540
chains of glucose.

7
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:22.160
So what makes those stems so tough?

8
00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.810
In this mission, you'll zoom from a single
cellulose chain up to a bundle called

9
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.280
a microfibril.

10
00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:30.900
Then you'll hang masses from real fibres,

11
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.670
and turn the snapping
point into a strength.

12
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:38.300
Your mission: find out what makes plant
stems tough enough to become linen and

13
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:38.840
rope.
